# Differential cases (ADR-0020) of #65 "S2a.15 Arithmetic and computed numbers": the equality depth of ADR-0029
# through array difference ([x] - [y] calls jv_equal(x, y); == is #66's), on both sides of 10 000. jq 1.8.2 checks
# the depth first on every call (depth > 10 000 raises "Equality check too deep"), then the kind, then identity
# (one value, or views of one document at one tape index, are equal without a walk); arrays compare elements at
# depth + 1; objects walk the LEFT object's keys in its order, a key missing on the right is false, and the sizes
# come last. jqj has no -s yet, so the two deep values are halves of one document [D, D], D being K nested arrays
# around 0 (a document nests 10 000 arrays at most, F-22; nested objects only 5 000, so the merge depth needs built
# values: the reduce cases at the end, recorded now and required by #69, and jq-core ObjectMergeDepthTest).
# [.[] | 1] prints [1] for a kept x and [] for a removed one. Written by a script; Format:
# oracle/src/main/java/io/github/subapavel/jqj/oracle/diff/DiffCase.java. Expected outputs live in arith-depth.rec,
# written by scripts/oracle-record.sh only. Ids are immutable.

# equal arrays on both sides of the bound

